# Project formatting standard.
#
# This codifies the style the firmware is already written in rather than
# imposing a new one, so running the formatter over the tree is close to a
# no-op and does not bury real changes in style churn.
#
# Zed and any other clangd-backed editor pick this up automatically, as does
# `make format` in software/.
#
# ColumnLimit 0 means "never reflow a line I did not ask you to reflow". That
# matters here: the ported TinyJoypad code has some very long expressions that
# are clearer left alone, and reflowing them would rewrite most of the game
# sources for no benefit.
#
# The sprite tables in software/src/spritebank.c are wrapped in
# `clang-format off`; they are hand-packed image data, not code.
#
# The ch32fun submodule carries its own .clang-format, which wins for its own
# files since clang-format uses the nearest config.

BasedOnStyle: LLVM
BreakBeforeBraces: Allman
IndentWidth: 2
ColumnLimit: 0
SortIncludes: false
AlignConsecutiveMacros: false
